error[E0277]: `Box<i64>` is not a storage of `Decimal`
 --> tests/ui/heap/boxed_native_is_not_a_decimal_storage.rs:8:13
  |
8 |   storage::<Box<i64>>();
  |             ^^^^^^^^ the trait `Storage` is not implemented for `Box<i64>`
  |
  = note: `Decimal` stores a native integer, `i8`, `i16`, `i32`, `i64`, `i128`, `u8`, `u16`, `u32`, `u64` or `u128`, or a wide integer, `i192`, `i256`, `i320`, `i384`, `i448`, `i512`, `i576`, `i640`, `i704`, `i768`, `i832`, `i896`, `i960`, `i1024`, `u192`, `u256`, `u320`, `u384`, `u448`, `u512`, `u576`, `u640`, `u704`, `u768`, `u832`, `u896`, `u960` or `u1024`
  = note: with the `std` or the `alloc` feature, `Decimal` also stores a wide integer whose limbs are in a `Box`, an `Rc` or an `Arc`, as in `Uint<U256, Box<[u64; 4]>>`, and with the `triomphe` feature one whose limbs are in a `triomphe::Arc`
  = help: the following other types implement trait `Storage`:
            Uint<B, Arc<[u64; N]>>
            Uint<B, Box<[u64; N]>>
            Uint<B, Rc<[u64; N]>>
            Uint<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UTerm, B1>, B0>, B0>, B0>, B0>, B0>, B0>, B0>, B0>, B0>, B0>, [u64; 16]>
            Uint<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UTerm, B1>, B0>, B0>, B0>, B0>, B0>, B0>, B0>, B0>, B0>, [u64; 8]>
            Uint<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UTerm, B1>, B0>, B0>, B1>, B0>, B0>, B0>, B0>, B0>, B0>, [u64; 9]>
            Uint<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UTerm, B1>, B0>, B1>, B0>, B0>, B0>, B0>, B0>, B0>, B0>, [u64; 10]>
            Uint<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UInt<UTerm, B1>, B0>, B1>, B1>, B0>, B0>, B0>, B0>, B0>, B0>, [u64; 11]>
          and $N others
